x − y = 6

What is the value of x?', '["14", "13", "26", "7"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Adding the equations gives 2x = 26, so x = 13.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_010', 'math', 1, 'Algebra', 'Linear inequalities', null, null, 'Which value of x is NOT a solution to x + 6 < 10?', '["−2", "4", "0", "3"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'x + 6 < 10 means x < 4. Since 4 is not less than 4, it is not a solution.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_011', 'math', 1, 'Algebra', 'Linear inequalities', null, null, 'Kim''s phone plan allows at most 500 minutes of calls per month. She has already used 320 minutes. Which inequality describes the number of minutes m she can still use this month?', '["m ≤ 180", "m ≥ 180", "m < 820", "m ≤ 820"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '320 + m ≤ 500, so m ≤ 180.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_012', 'math', 1, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is equivalent to 3(x + 4) − 2x?', '["5x + 12", "x + 10", "x + 4", "x + 12"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '3x + 12 − 2x = x + 12.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_013', 'math', 1, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is equivalent to (x^{4})^{3}?', '["x^{64}", "x^{12}", "x^{7}", "3x^{4}"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'When raising a power to a power, multiply the exponents: 4 × 3 = 12.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_014', 'math', 1, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is equivalent to x(x + 6)?', '["x^{2} + 6x", "x^{2} + 6", "2x + 6", "7x"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Multiply x by each term: x · x + x · 6 = x^{2} + 6x.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_015', 'math', 1, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is a factored form of x^{2} − 25?', '["(x − 5)^{2}", "(x − 25)(x + 1)", "(x + 5)^{2}", "(x − 5)(x + 5)"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'x^{2} − 25 is a difference of squares: (x − 5)(x + 5).', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_016', 'math', 1, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'If 5x^{2} = 80 and x > 0, what is the value of x?', null, null, '["4"]'::jsonb, 'Divide by 5: x^{2} = 16, so x = 4.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_017', 'math', 1, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'What are the solutions to x^{2} − 7x = 0?', '["x = 0 and x = 7", "x = 7 only", "x = 0 only", "x = −7 and x = 0"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Factor: x(x − 7) = 0, so x = 0 or x = 7.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_018', 'math', 1, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'The function f is defined by f(x) = x^{2} + 2x. What is f(−3)?', '["3", "15", "−3", "−15"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'f(−3) = 9 − 6 = 3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_019', 'math', 1, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'A bacteria colony starts with 50 cells and triples every hour. How many cells are there after 2 hours?', '["450", "1,350", "300", "150"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '50 × 3 × 3 = 450.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_020', 'math', 1, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'Which point is on the graph of y = x^{2} − 4?', '["(2, 4)", "(0, 4)", "(3, 5)", "(1, 3)"]'::jsonb, 2, null, '3^{2} − 4 = 5, so (3, 5) is on the graph.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_021', 'math', 1, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'Which describes the graph of y = −x^{2}?', '["A parabola that opens upward", "A horizontal line", "A straight line with slope −1", "A parabola that opens downward"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The negative coefficient of x^{2} makes the parabola open downward.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_022', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'A printer prints 18 pages per minute. How many pages does it print in 7 minutes?', '["25", "140", "108", "126"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '18 × 7 = 126.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_023', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'Three notebooks cost $7.50. At this rate, how much do 8 notebooks cost, in dollars?', null, null, '["20"]'::jsonb, 'Each notebook costs 7.50 ÷ 3 = 2.50, and 8 × 2.50 = 20.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_024', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'How many hours are in 3 days?', '["60", "48", "72", "36"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Each day has 24 hours: 3 × 24 = 72.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_025', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, 'What is 8% of 350?', '["280", "28", "2.8", "42"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '0.08 × 350 = 28.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_026', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, 'A $60 sweater is on sale for 25% off. What is the sale price, in dollars?', null, null, '["45"]'::jsonb, '25% of 60 is 15, so the sale price is 60 − 15 = 45.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_027', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, 'In a class, 18 of 24 students passed a quiz. What percent passed?', '["18%", "80%", "24%", "75%"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '18 ÷ 24 = 0.75 = 75%.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_028', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'One-variable data', null, null, 'What is the mean of 4, 9, 10, and 13?', '["10", "9", "36", "9.5"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The sum is 36, and 36 ÷ 4 = 9.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_029', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'One-variable data', null, null, 'What is the range of the data set 14, 3, 22, 9, 17?', null, null, '["19"]'::jsonb, 'Range = greatest − least = 22 − 3 = 19.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_030', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Two-variable data', null, '{"h": ["x", "y"], "r": [["1", "5"], ["2", "8"], ["3", "11"]]}'::jsonb, 'Which equation fits all the values in the table?', '["y = 3x + 2", "y = 2x + 3", "y = 5x", "y = x + 4"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'y increases by 3 each time x increases by 1, and 3(1) + 2 = 5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_031', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Probability and conditional probability', null, null, 'One letter is chosen at random from the word MATH. What is the probability that it is a vowel?', '["1/3", "1/2", "1/4", "3/4"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Only A is a vowel: 1 out of 4 letters.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_032', 'math', 1, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Inference from sample statistics', null, null, 'A school has 600 students. In a random sample of 40 students, 10 said soccer is their favorite sport. Based on the sample, about how many students at the school would say soccer is their favorite?', '["60", "10", "150", "240"]'::jsonb, 2, null, '10/40 = 25%, and 25% of 600 is 150.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_033', 'math', 1, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Area and volume', null, null, 'A rectangle is 8 meters wide and 13 meters long. What is its area, in square meters?', '["104", "96", "21", "42"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '8 × 13 = 104.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_034', 'math', 1, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Area and volume', null, null, 'A circle has a radius of 3. What is its area?', '["6π", "18π", "9π", "3π"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Area = πr^{2} = 9π.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_035', 'math', 1, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Area and volume', null, null, 'A box is 3 inches wide, 4 inches long, and 10 inches tall. What is its volume, in cubic inches?', null, null, '["120"]'::jsonb, '3 × 4 × 10 = 120.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_036', 'math', 1, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Lines, angles, and triangles', null, null, 'A right triangle has one angle that measures 35°. What is the measure of its other acute angle?', '["55°", "45°", "125°", "65°"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The angles add to 180°: 180 − 90 − 35 = 55.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_037', 'math', 1, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Lines, angles, and triangles', null, null, 'What is the measure, in degrees, of the complement of a 63° angle?', null, null, '["27"]'::jsonb, 'Complementary angles add to 90°: 90 − 63 = 27.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_038', 'math', 1, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Lines, angles, and triangles', null, null, 'Two angles form a straight line. One measures x° and the other measures 3x°. What is the value of x?', '["30", "60", "135", "45"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'x + 3x = 180, so 4x = 180 and x = 45.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_039', 'math', 1, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Right triangles and trigonometry', null, null, 'A right triangle has legs of length 8 and 15. What is the length of the hypotenuse?', null, null, '["17"]'::jsonb, '8^{2} + 15^{2} = 64 + 225 = 289, and √289 = 17.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl1f_040', 'math', 1, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Circles', null, null, 'A circle has a circumference of 16π. What is its diameter?', '["4", "16", "8", "32"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Circumference = π × diameter, so the diameter is 16.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_001', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear equations in one variable', null, null, 'If 2(3x − 1) − (x + 4) = 9, what is the value of x?', null, null, '["3"]'::jsonb, '6x − 2 − x − 4 = 9, so 5x − 6 = 9, 5x = 15 and x = 3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_002', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear equations in one variable', null, null, 'If 4x + 7 = 31, what is the value of 2x − 1?', '["6", "11", "23", "12"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '4x = 24, so x = 6 and 2x − 1 = 11.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_003', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear equations in one variable', null, null, 'If (x + 3)/5 = (x − 1)/3, what is the value of x?', '["2", "−7", "7", "4"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Cross-multiply: 3(x + 3) = 5(x − 1), so 3x + 9 = 5x − 5, 14 = 2x and x = 7.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_004', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear equations in one variable', null, null, 'A phone plan costs $35 per month plus a one-time $50 activation fee. After how many months will the total cost be $330?', null, null, '["8"]'::jsonb, '50 + 35m = 330, so 35m = 280 and m = 8.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_005', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear functions', null, null, 'A line passes through (0, −3) and (4, 5). Which equation represents the line?', '["y = 2x + 5", "y = 2x − 3", "y = −3x + 2", "y = (1/2)x − 3"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The slope is (5 − (−3)) ÷ 4 = 2, and the y-intercept is −3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_006', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear functions', null, null, 'The function f is defined by f(x) = −3x + b, where b is a constant. If f(2) = 4, what is f(−1)?', null, null, '["13"]'::jsonb, '−6 + b = 4, so b = 10. Then f(−1) = 3 + 10 = 13.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_007', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear functions', null, null, 'A tank holds 500 liters of water and drains at 20 liters per minute. Which function gives the volume V, in liters, after t minutes?', '["V = 480t", "V = 500t − 20", "V = 20t − 500", "V = 500 − 20t"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Start at 500 and subtract 20 for each minute.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_008', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear functions', null, null, 'What is the x-intercept of the graph of 3x − 4y = 24?', '["(8, 0)", "(−8, 0)", "(−6, 0)", "(0, −6)"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Set y = 0: 3x = 24, so x = 8.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_009', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Systems of linear equations', null, null, '3x + y = 14
x + 2y = 13

What is the value of y?', null, null, '["5"]'::jsonb, 'From the first equation, y = 14 − 3x. Substituting: x + 28 − 6x = 13, so x = 3 and y = 5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_010', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Systems of linear equations', null, null, '5x − 2y = 4
3x + 2y = 12

What is the value of x + y?', '["7", "3", "2", "5"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Adding gives 8x = 16, so x = 2. Then 6 + 2y = 12, so y = 3, and x + y = 5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_011', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Systems of linear equations', null, null, 'A theater sold 300 tickets. Adult tickets cost $12 and student tickets cost $8, and ticket sales totaled $3,040. How many student tickets were sold?', '["120", "140", "160", "180"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'a + s = 300 and 12a + 8s = 3,040. Substituting a = 300 − s: 3,600 − 4s = 3,040, so s = 140.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_012', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Systems of linear equations', null, null, 'How many solutions does this system have?

y = 2x + 3
4x − 2y = −6', '["Exactly two", "Infinitely many", "Zero", "Exactly one"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Solving the second equation for y gives y = 2x + 3, the same line as the first.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_013', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear inequalities', null, null, 'Which describes all solutions to 3(x − 2) ≥ 5x + 4?', '["x ≤ −5", "x ≤ 5", "x ≥ 5", "x ≥ −5"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '3x − 6 ≥ 5x + 4 gives −10 ≥ 2x, so x ≤ −5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_014', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear inequalities', null, null, 'An elevator can carry at most 2,000 pounds. Nine people with an average weight of 170 pounds are inside. What is the greatest number of 50-pound boxes that can be added?', null, null, '["9"]'::jsonb, 'The people weigh 9 × 170 = 1,530 pounds, leaving 470 pounds. 470 ÷ 50 = 9.4, so at most 9 boxes.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_015', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is equivalent to (x + 5)(2x − 3)?', '["2x^{2} − 15", "2x^{2} + 13x − 15", "2x^{2} + 7x − 15", "2x^{2} − 7x − 15"]'::jsonb, 2, null, '2x^{2} − 3x + 10x − 15 = 2x^{2} + 7x − 15.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_016', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is a factored form of 25x^{2} − 1?', '["(5x − 1)^{2}", "(5x − 1)(5x + 1)", "(25x − 1)(x + 1)", "5(5x^{2} − 1)"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '25x^{2} − 1 is a difference of squares: (5x)^{2} − 1^{2}.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_017', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is equivalent to (6x^{3}y^{2})/(2xy), for x ≠ 0 and y ≠ 0?', '["3x^{2}y", "3xy", "3x^{3}y^{2}", "4x^{2}y"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '6 ÷ 2 = 3, x^{3} ÷ x = x^{2}, and y^{2} ÷ y = y.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_018', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is equivalent to √(x^{8}), for x > 0?', '["x^{16}", "x^{6}", "x^{4}", "x^{2}"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Taking a square root halves the exponent: 8 ÷ 2 = 4.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_019', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'What is the negative solution of x^{2} + 5x − 14 = 0?', null, null, '["-7", "−7"]'::jsonb, '(x + 7)(x − 2) = 0, so x = −7 or x = 2.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_020', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'If 3^{2x} = 81, what is the value of x?', '["3", "27", "4", "2"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '81 = 3^{4}, so 2x = 4 and x = 2.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_021', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'What are the solutions to 2x^{2} = 50?', '["x = 5 and x = −5", "x = √50 only", "x = 5 only", "x = 25 and x = −25"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'x^{2} = 25, so x = 5 or x = −5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_022', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'What is the larger solution of (x − 1)^{2} = 16?', null, null, '["5"]'::jsonb, 'x − 1 = 4 or x − 1 = −4, so x = 5 or x = −3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_023', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'If 1/x + 1/3 = 1/2, what is the value of x?', '["6", "5", "1/6", "3"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '1/x = 1/2 − 1/3 = 1/6, so x = 6.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_024', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'The function f is defined by f(x) = −(x + 2)^{2} + 7. What is the maximum value of f?', '["−2", "2", "−7", "7"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '−(x + 2)^{2} is never positive and equals 0 at x = −2, so the maximum is 7.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_025', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'A $1,500 deposit earns 4% interest compounded once a year. Which expression gives its value after t years?', '["1,500(0.04)^{t}", "1,500 + 0.04t", "1,500(1.04)^{t}", "1,500(1.4)^{t}"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Each year the value is multiplied by 1 + 0.04 = 1.04.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_026', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'The function f is defined by f(x) = x^{2} − 2x. Which expression is equivalent to f(a + 1)?', '["a^{2} − 2a + 1", "a^{2} − 1", "a^{2} − 2a", "a^{2} + 1"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '(a + 1)^{2} − 2(a + 1) = a^{2} + 2a + 1 − 2a − 2 = a^{2} − 1.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_027', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'What is the x-coordinate of the vertex of the graph of y = (x − 4)(x + 2)?', null, null, '["1"]'::jsonb, 'The zeros are 4 and −2, and the vertex is halfway between them: (4 + (−2)) ÷ 2 = 1.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_028', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'Concrete is mixed using 1 part cement to 3 parts sand by volume. How many cubic feet of cement are in 24 cubic feet of the mix?', '["8", "6", "18", "3"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The mix has 1 + 3 = 4 parts, so cement is 24 ÷ 4 = 6 cubic feet.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_029', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'A train travels 150 kilometers in 1.25 hours. What is its average speed, in kilometers per hour?', null, null, '["120"]'::jsonb, '150 ÷ 1.25 = 120.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_030', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'A faucet drips 3 milliliters of water every 10 seconds. How many liters does it drip in one day? (1 day = 86,400 seconds; 1 liter = 1,000 milliliters)', '["43.2", "25.92", "2.592", "259.2"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '3 ÷ 10 × 86,400 = 25,920 mL, which is 25.92 liters.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_031', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, 'After a 20% discount, a pair of shoes costs $56. What was the original price, in dollars?', null, null, '["70"]'::jsonb, '0.80P = 56, so P = 70.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_032', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, 'A town''s population of 4,000 grows by 5% each year. What will the population be after 2 years?', '["4,410", "4,800", "4,400", "4,200"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '4,000 × 1.05 × 1.05 = 4,410.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_033', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, '28 is what percent of 80?', '["28%", "52%", "35%", "2.86%"]'::jsonb, 2, null, '28 ÷ 80 = 0.35 = 35%.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_034', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'One-variable data', null, null, 'The mean of 7 numbers is 12. When an 8th number is added, the mean becomes 13. What is the 8th number?', null, null, '["20"]'::jsonb, 'The total goes from 7 × 12 = 84 to 8 × 13 = 104, so the 8th number is 20.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_035', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'One-variable data', null, null, 'For the data set 5, 7, 8, 12, 13, 14, 20, the first quartile is 7 and the third quartile is 14. What is the interquartile range?', '["7", "12", "15", "6"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'IQR = Q3 − Q1 = 14 − 7 = 7.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_036', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'One-variable data', null, null, 'Each of the 10 values in a data set is increased by 3. What happens to the mean?', '["It stays the same", "It triples", "It increases by 30", "It increases by 3"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Adding 3 to every value adds 30 to the total, and 30 ÷ 10 = 3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_037', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Two-variable data', null, null, 'The line of best fit y = −1.5x + 90 predicts a student''s quiz score y from x, the number of hours of TV the student watches per week. What is the predicted score for a student who watches 12 hours?', null, null, '["72"]'::jsonb, '−1.5(12) + 90 = 72.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_038', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Two-variable data', null, '{"h": ["Years (x)", "Value (y), $"], "r": [["0", "24,000"], ["1", "20,400"], ["2", "17,340"]]}'::jsonb, 'The table shows a car''s value over time. Which equation best models the data?', '["y = 24,000(1.15)^{x}", "y = 24,000(0.85)^{x}", "y = 24,000(0.15)^{x}", "y = 24,000 − 3,600x"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Each value is 85% of the one before: 24,000 × 0.85 = 20,400 and 20,400 × 0.85 = 17,340.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_039', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Probability and conditional probability', null, '{"h": ["", "Fiction", "Nonfiction"], "r": [["Grade 11", "45", "30"], ["Grade 12", "35", "40"]]}'::jsonb, 'The table shows the reading preferences of 150 students.

If a grade 12 student is chosen at random, what is the probability that the student prefers nonfiction?', '["4/15", "7/15", "4/7", "8/15"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'There are 35 + 40 = 75 grade 12 students, and 40 prefer nonfiction: 40/75 = 8/15.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_040', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Probability and conditional probability', null, null, 'A spinner with 5 equal sections numbered 1 to 5 is spun twice. What is the probability that both results are even?', '["4/25", "2/25", "2/5", "4/5"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Two of five numbers are even, so the probability is (2/5)(2/5) = 4/25.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_041', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Inference from sample statistics', null, null, 'A poll of 500 randomly chosen voters found that 46% support a proposal, with a margin of error of 4 percentage points. Can you conclude that a majority of all voters support it?', '["No; the plausible range, 42% to 50%, does not include a majority", "No, because no conclusion can ever be drawn from a sample", "Yes, because the sample was random", "Yes, because 46% is close to 50%"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '46% ± 4% gives 42% to 50%. A majority would need more than 50%.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_042', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Area and volume', null, null, 'A figure is made of a 12-by-8 rectangle with a semicircle attached to one of its 8-unit sides. What is the total area of the figure?', '["96 + 16π", "96 + 64π", "96 + 8π", "96 + 4π"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Rectangle: 96. Semicircle with radius 4: (1/2)π(16) = 8π.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_043', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Area and volume', null, null, 'A cylinder has a volume of 200π and a radius of 5. What is its height?', null, null, '["8"]'::jsonb, 'π(25)h = 200π, so h = 8.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_044', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Lines, angles, and triangles', null, null, 'What is the measure of each exterior angle of a regular pentagon?', '["36°", "60°", "108°", "72°"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The exterior angles of any polygon add to 360°, and 360 ÷ 5 = 72.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_045', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Lines, angles, and triangles', null, null, 'The angles of a triangle measure (x + 10)°, (2x)°, and (3x − 10)°. What is the value of x?', null, null, '["30"]'::jsonb, 'x + 10 + 2x + 3x − 10 = 6x = 180, so x = 30.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_046', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Lines, angles, and triangles', null, null, 'Two triangles are similar. A side of the smaller triangle is 6, and the corresponding side of the larger triangle is 15. The smaller triangle''s perimeter is 22. What is the larger triangle''s perimeter?', '["82.5", "37", "55", "31"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The scale factor is 15 ÷ 6 = 2.5, so the perimeter is 22 × 2.5 = 55.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_047', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Right triangles and trigonometry', null, null, 'In a right triangle, cos A = 0.6 and the hypotenuse is 25. What is the length of the side adjacent to angle A?', '["20", "9", "10", "15"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'cos A = adjacent ÷ hypotenuse, so adjacent = 0.6 × 25 = 15.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_048', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Right triangles and trigonometry', null, null, 'In right triangle ABC, angle C is the right angle, AC = 9, and BC = 12. What is sin A?', '["4/3", "3/5", "3/4", "4/5"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The hypotenuse AB is 15. The side opposite A is BC = 12, so sin A = 12/15 = 4/5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_049', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Circles', null, null, 'Which point lies on the circle x^{2} + (y − 3)^{2} = 20?', '["(4, 3)", "(2, 3)", "(2, 7)", "(0, 20)"]'::jsonb, 2, null, '2^{2} + (7 − 3)^{2} = 4 + 16 = 20.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2f_050', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Circles', null, null, 'A circle has a radius of 6. What is the area of a sector with a central angle of 120°?', '["24π", "36π", "12π", "4π"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The sector is 120/360 = 1/3 of the circle''s area 36π, which is 12π.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_001', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Linear equations in one variable', null, null, 'If 5/(x + 1) = 2/(x − 2), and x ≠ −1 and x ≠ 2, what is the value of x?', '["8/3", "2", "−4", "4"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Cross-multiply: 5(x − 2) = 2(x + 1), so 5x − 10 = 2x + 2, 3x = 12 and x = 4.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_002', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Linear equations in one variable', null, null, 'In the equation kx − 3 = 2(x + 4), k is a constant. For what value of k does the equation have no solution?', '["2", "−2", "3", "8"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'kx − 3 = 2x + 8. When k = 2, the x terms cancel and −3 = 8 is false, so there is no solution.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_003', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Linear equations in one variable', null, null, 'If (a + b)/b = 7/3, what is the value of a/b?', null, null, '["4/3", "1.333"]'::jsonb, '(a + b)/b = a/b + 1 = 7/3, so a/b = 4/3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_004', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Linear functions', null, null, 'The function f is defined by f(x) = ax + b, where a > 0. If f(f(x)) = 9x − 8 for all x, what is the value of b?', null, null, '["-2", "−2"]'::jsonb, 'f(f(x)) = a(ax + b) + b = a^{2}x + ab + b. So a^{2} = 9, giving a = 3, and 3b + b = −8, giving b = −2.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_005', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Linear functions', null, null, 'A line passes through (2, −1) and (k, 7) and has slope 4. What is the value of k?', '["3", "4", "6", "2"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '(7 − (−1))/(k − 2) = 4, so 8 = 4(k − 2) and k = 4.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_006', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Linear functions', null, null, 'Air temperature drops about 3.5°F for every 1,000 feet of elevation gained. If the temperature is 68°F at sea level, at about what elevation, in feet, will the temperature be 40°F?', '["11,400", "9,500", "6,000", "8,000"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The drop is 68 − 40 = 28°F, and 28 ÷ 3.5 = 8 thousands of feet.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_007', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Systems of linear equations', null, null, '(1/2)x + y = 5
3x − 2y = 6

If (x, y) is the solution to the system, what is the value of 2x + y?', null, null, '["11"]'::jsonb, 'Double the first equation: x + 2y = 10. Adding to the second gives 4x = 16, so x = 4 and y = 3. Then 2x + y = 11.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_008', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Systems of linear equations', null, null, 'rx + 4y = 10
6x + 8y = s

In the system, r and s are constants. If the system has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of r + s?', '["23", "26", "10", "13"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The second equation must be 2 times the first: 6 = 2r and s = 20. So r = 3 and r + s = 23.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_009', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Systems of linear equations', null, null, 'Ingrid invests $10,000, part at 4% annual interest and the rest at 6%. After one year she has earned $520 in interest. How much did she invest at 6%, in dollars?', '["8,000", "6,000", "5,200", "4,000"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '0.04(10,000 − y) + 0.06y = 520 gives 400 + 0.02y = 520, so y = 6,000.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_010', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Linear inequalities', null, null, 'Which point (x, y) satisfies both y ≥ 3x − 5 and y < −x + 4?', '["(2, 2)", "(−1, 6)", "(1, 0)", "(3, 3)"]'::jsonb, 2, null, '(1, 0): 0 ≥ −2 and 0 < 3. (2, 2) fails 2 < 2; (3, 3) fails 3 ≥ 4; (−1, 6) fails 6 < 5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_011', 'math', 3, 'Algebra', 'Linear inequalities', null, null, 'If x and y are positive integers and 3x + 5y ≤ 30, what is the greatest possible value of x + y?', null, null, '["9"]'::jsonb, 'Since x costs less than y, make y as small as possible: y = 1 gives 3x ≤ 25, so x = 8 and x + y = 9. Larger y values give smaller sums.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_012', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'If x^{2} − y^{2} = 48 and x + y = 8, what is the value of x − y?', '["40", "384", "6", "56"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'x^{2} − y^{2} = (x + y)(x − y), so 8(x − y) = 48 and x − y = 6.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_013', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is equivalent to (2x^{2} + 5x − 3)/(x + 3), for x ≠ −3?', '["2x − 1", "2x − 3", "x − 1", "2x + 1"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '2x^{2} + 5x − 3 = (x + 3)(2x − 1), so the quotient is 2x − 1.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_014', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'What is the value of 8^{2/3} · 4^{−1/2}?', null, null, '["2"]'::jsonb, '8^{2/3} = (∛8)^{2} = 4 and 4^{−1/2} = 1/2. Their product is 2.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_015', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is equivalent to (a^{−2}b^{3})/(a^{4}b^{−1}), for a ≠ 0 and b ≠ 0?', '["b^{2}/a^{2}", "b^{4}/a^{6}", "b^{4}/a^{2}", "a^{6}b^{4}"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Exponents of a: −2 − 4 = −6. Exponents of b: 3 − (−1) = 4.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_016', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'The equation x^{2} + bx + 12 = 0 has solutions 2 and r. What is the value of b?', '["8", "−14", "−8", "−6"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The product of the solutions is 12, so r = 6. Their sum, 8, equals −b, so b = −8.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_017', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'What is the solution to x − 4 = √(x − 2)?', '["6", "3", "3 and 6", "2"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Squaring: x^{2} − 8x + 16 = x − 2, so x^{2} − 9x + 18 = 0 and x = 3 or 6. At x = 3, the left side is −1 but the right is 1, so 3 is extraneous.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_018', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'The graphs of y = x^{2} + 2x and y = 4x + k intersect at exactly one point. What is the value of k?', null, null, '["-1", "−1"]'::jsonb, 'x^{2} + 2x = 4x + k gives x^{2} − 2x − k = 0. One solution means the discriminant is 0: 4 + 4k = 0, so k = −1.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_019', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'If 5^{x} · 25^{x + 1} = 125^{2}, what is the value of x?', null, null, '["4/3", "1.333"]'::jsonb, 'Write as powers of 5: 5^{x} · 5^{2x + 2} = 5^{6}. So 3x + 2 = 6 and x = 4/3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_020', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'What is the solution to (x^{2} − 4)/(x − 2) = 7?', '["5", "3", "There is no solution", "9"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'For x ≠ 2, (x^{2} − 4)/(x − 2) = x + 2. Then x + 2 = 7, so x = 5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_021', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'A ball''s height, in meters, t seconds after it is thrown is h(t) = −5t^{2} + 20t + 25. After how many seconds does the ball hit the ground?', null, null, '["5"]'::jsonb, '−5(t^{2} − 4t − 5) = −5(t − 5)(t + 1) = 0, so t = 5 (time can''t be negative).', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_022', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'The function f is defined by f(x) = 3(2)^{x}. What is the value of f(x + 2)/f(x)?', '["2", "12", "6", "4"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'f(x + 2)/f(x) = 2^{x + 2}/2^{x} = 2^{2} = 4.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_023', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'A substance loses half its mass every 6 hours. A sample has a mass of 80 grams. After how many hours will its mass be 10 grams?', '["12", "24", "18", "30"]'::jsonb, 2, null, '80 → 40 → 20 → 10 takes 3 halvings, or 3 × 6 = 18 hours.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_024', 'math', 3, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'A parabola has its vertex at (−1, 5) and passes through (1, −3). What is the y-intercept of the parabola?', '["(0, −3)", "(0, 1)", "(0, 3)", "(0, 5)"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'y = a(x + 1)^{2} + 5. Using (1, −3): 4a + 5 = −3, so a = −2. At x = 0: −2 + 5 = 3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_025', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'Two meshing gears have 36 teeth and 24 teeth. When the larger gear makes 40 full turns, how many full turns does the smaller gear make?', null, null, '["60"]'::jsonb, 'The same number of teeth pass: 36 × 40 = 1,440, and 1,440 ÷ 24 = 60.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_026', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'Car A leaves a town driving 60 miles per hour. One hour later, car B leaves the same town on the same road driving 75 miles per hour. How many hours after car B leaves will it catch up to car A?', '["3", "6", "5", "4"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '75t = 60(t + 1) gives 15t = 60, so t = 4.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_027', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'A city of 2.4 million people covers 300 square miles. What is its population density, in people per square mile?', '["80,000", "8,000", "800", "720"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '2,400,000 ÷ 300 = 8,000.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_028', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, 'A stock''s price falls by 25%. By what percent must the new price rise to return to the original price?', '["25%", "75%", "33 1/3%", "20%"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'If the price was 100, it falls to 75. Rising 25 from 75 is 25/75 = 33 1/3%.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_029', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, 'Of the 800 students at a school, 45% play a sport. Of those, 30% play two sports. How many students play two sports?', null, null, '["108"]'::jsonb, '0.45 × 800 = 360 play a sport, and 0.30 × 360 = 108.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_030', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'One-variable data', null, null, 'A data set of 15 values has a mean of 40. Three values with a mean of 30 are removed. What is the mean of the remaining values?', '["45", "40", "50", "42.5"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The total falls from 600 to 600 − 90 = 510, and 510 ÷ 12 = 42.5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_031', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'One-variable data', null, null, 'Which change to the data set 3, 5, 8, 10, 14 would increase its median?', '["Replacing 8 with 9", "Replacing 5 with 7", "Replacing 3 with 1", "Replacing 14 with 30"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The median is the middle value, 8. Only changing that value to 9 raises it; the other changes leave 8 in the middle.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_032', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Two-variable data', null, null, 'A model predicts y = 1.2x + 4. For one observation, x = 10 and y = 19. What is the residual (observed minus predicted) for this observation?', null, null, '["3"]'::jsonb, 'Predicted: 1.2(10) + 4 = 16. Residual: 19 − 16 = 3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_033', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Probability and conditional probability', null, '{"h": ["", "Vaccinated", "Not vaccinated"], "r": [["Got flu", "12", "48"], ["No flu", "288", "152"]]}'::jsonb, 'The table shows flu cases among 500 people during one winter.

If a person who got the flu is chosen at random, what is the probability that the person was not vaccinated?', '["6/25", "4/5", "1/5", "12/125"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '12 + 48 = 60 people got the flu, and 48 were not vaccinated: 48/60 = 4/5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_034', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Probability and conditional probability', null, null, 'Two different cards are drawn at random from five cards numbered 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5. What is the probability that their sum is 7?', '["4/25", "1/5", "2/25", "1/10"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'There are 10 possible pairs, and two of them, {2, 5} and {3, 4}, sum to 7: 2/10 = 1/5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_035', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Inference from sample statistics', null, null, 'A study found that students who eat breakfast tend to have higher test scores than students who don''t. The students were not randomly assigned to eat breakfast. Which conclusion is best supported?', '["Eating breakfast is associated with higher scores, but the study does not show that it causes them", "Higher test scores cause students to eat breakfast", "Eating breakfast has no relationship with test scores", "Eating breakfast causes higher test scores"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Without random assignment, the study shows an association, not cause and effect.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_036', 'math', 3, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Inference from sample statistics', null, null, 'A random sample of 1,000 adults in one state found that 28% exercise daily. To which group can this result most reasonably be generalized?', '["All people in the state, including children", "Adults in that state", "Only the 1,000 adults surveyed", "All adults in the country"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'A random sample represents the population it was drawn from: adults in that state.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_037', 'math', 3, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Area and volume', null, null, 'What is the area of an equilateral triangle with sides of length 10?', '["25√3", "50", "50√3", "100√3/3"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The height is 5√3, so the area is (1/2)(10)(5√3) = 25√3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_038', 'math', 3, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Area and volume', null, null, 'A sphere has a volume of 288π. What is its radius?', null, null, '["6"]'::jsonb, '(4/3)πr^{3} = 288π, so r^{3} = 216 and r = 6.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_039', 'math', 3, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Area and volume', null, null, 'A cylinder''s radius is doubled and its height is cut in half. By what factor does its volume change?', '["4", "1", "1/2", "2"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'V = πr^{2}h. Doubling r multiplies V by 4, and halving h divides by 2, for a factor of 2.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_040', 'math', 3, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Lines, angles, and triangles', null, null, 'A triangle has sides of length 5, 12, and x, where x is an integer. How many values of x are possible?', null, null, '["9"]'::jsonb, 'By the triangle inequality, 12 − 5 < x < 12 + 5, so 7 < x < 17. The integers 8 through 16 give 9 values.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_041', 'math', 3, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Lines, angles, and triangles', null, null, 'Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. Two same-side interior angles measure (4x + 20)° and (2x + 40)°. What is the measure of the smaller angle?', '["100°", "60°", "20°", "80°"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Same-side interior angles are supplementary: 6x + 60 = 180, so x = 20. The angles are 100° and 80°.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_042', 'math', 3, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Right triangles and trigonometry', null, null, 'Angle θ is between 90° and 180°, and sin θ = 5/13. What is cos θ?', '["−5/12", "5/12", "−12/13", "12/13"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'sin^{2}θ + cos^{2}θ = 1 gives cos θ = ±12/13. Cosine is negative between 90° and 180°.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_043', 'math', 3, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Right triangles and trigonometry', null, null, 'In right triangle ABC, angles A and B are the acute angles. If sin A = (2x + 1)/10 and cos B = (3x − 4)/10, what is the value of x?', null, null, '["5"]'::jsonb, 'In a right triangle, sin A = cos B. So 2x + 1 = 3x − 4 and x = 5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_044', 'math', 3, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Circles', null, null, 'A circle in the xy-plane has its center at (3, −4) and passes through the origin. Which equation represents the circle?', '["(x − 3)^{2} + (y + 4)^{2} = 5", "(x − 3)^{2} + (y + 4)^{2} = 25", "(x + 3)^{2} + (y − 4)^{2} = 25", "(x − 3)^{2} + (y − 4)^{2} = 25"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The radius is the distance from (3, −4) to (0, 0): √(9 + 16) = 5, so r^{2} = 25.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl3f_045', 'math', 3, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Circles', null, null, 'An arc of a circle with radius 9 has length 6π. What is the measure, in degrees, of the arc''s central angle?', null, null, '["120"]'::jsonb, 'The circumference is 18π, and 6π is one-third of it, so the angle is 360 ÷ 3 = 120.', 'published', 'import', now())
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- Fixes to two round-7 questions (safe to re-run).
update public.ascend_questions
   set explanation = 'Cheering, singing, a trophy, and a smiling coach are signs of a win.'
 where id = 'rwl1e_028';
update public.ascend_questions
   set skill = 'Form, Structure, and Sense',
       explanation = 'The studio belongs to one artist, so the singular possessive "artist''s" is correct.'
 where id = 'rwl3e_033';
